Once upon a time, there was a little boy named Tim. Tim loved to play with his toy cars. One day, Tim's mom said, "Tim, we need to mail a letter to grandma. Can you help me?"
Tim was very excited to help. He took his toy cars and went to the post office. On the way, he saw a big puddle. Tim thought it would be fun to jump in it. But, he did not see the water on the ground.
Tim ran into the puddle and his toy cars went up and down. He laughed and said, "I am going to mail a letter too!" Then, he saw a small box with a picture of a cake on it. Tim thought it was his grandma's cake. He put the letter in the box and went back to the post office to mail it.
When Tim got to the post office, he saw that the box was open. He ran to the box and opened it. Inside, he found a big, wet toy car. Tim was very happy. He played with the toy car all day and forgot about the puddle and the letter.
